k and Wiliam, 1998). Other educators also soon began to espouse the merits of formative assessment and its impact on greater student understanding (Smith and Gorard, 2005).\n\nWhile studies have shown positive impacts that can occur with localized formative assessments originating in a classroom setting, there may be greater promise in developing testing systems that encompass the cohesive additions of summative exams as well. One of the benefits of a more complete, robust testing system that bridges the gap between formative and summative assessments is that better tests not only increase",
