alysis was used to explore the nature and frequency of teachers' use of peer and self-assessment. Results showed that 24% of the teachers reported that they did not use those strategies. They reported different reasons such high school students' capability of being truthful and objective in self and peerassessment. 49% reported they used these strategies 'a little', 5% used them 'seldom' and 27% reported using strategies 'somewhat'. Teachers who reported using strategies 'a little' mentioned that these strategies facilitate students' reflection on their achievement.",
