      "snippet": {
        "text": "Formative assessment techniques have a strong positive relationship with student learning and academic achievement (Kausar, 2022). \n\nFurther research shows that formative assessment is highly effective in improving learning outcomes because it focuses on continuous development through feedback (Voinea, 2018). Formative assessment, especially when integrated with student response systems (SRS), significantly improves learning outcomes (Ngo Van, 2021). Formative assessment, especially through test follow-up strategies, effectively improves student learning outcomes in test-dominated contexts (Xiao, 2017). Effectiveness of formative assessment in improving students' cognitive development and learning outcomes (Savinykh, 2022). Formative assessment is highly effective in improving learning outcomes because it reinforces student learning and can significantly improve student achievement while informing daily classroom practices (Staunton & Dann, 2016). Formative assessment has been shown to improve learning outcomes for all students, especially those who struggle with learning and students with disabilities (Nikolaevna Shapovalova & Efremova, 2020). There was a significant improvement in students' academic performance after implementing formative assessment (Arja et al., 2018). Research shows that formative assessment significantly improves student learning outcomes by familiarizing students with the level of learning required, identifying gaps, and providing constructive feedback (Evans et al., 2014). The use of quality formative assessments significantly improves students' perceptions of self-directed learning, leading to improved learning outcomes (Weldmeskel & Dreyer, 2016). \n\nFormative assessment is effective in improving learning outcomes by providing ongoing feedback that helps students understand their learning goals and progress (Vonderwell & Boboc, 2013). The mobile learning approach based on formative assessment significantly improves students' learning achievement and attitudes (Hwang & Chang, 2011). Formative assessment significantly impacts teaching practice by facilitating the interpretation of learning and teaching (Montaño Oñate et al., 2024). Formative assessment has a positive impact on student learning outcomes by improving competency (Khursheed & Shahid, 2023). Formative assessment is effective in improving learning outcomes because it provides constructive and informative feedback, allowing students to identify and improve their shortcomings (Magdalena et al., 2023).",
