swers in the exams. Yet, the formative feedback given by the teacher is vital if students are to carry out and manage the learning process correctly. The purpose of formative feedback is to provide the person with the power to supervise and direct their own learning so that the person can be a more determined, responsible, and effective learner (Black & Jones, 2006). This explanation reveals the relationship between formative feedback and self-regulated learning. Butler and Winne (1995) stated that feedback is",
