d relevance, the final 30 articles were selected based on strict inclusion and exclusion criteria. Inclusion criteria included articles that discussed the direct relationship between formative assessment and learning outcomes, used a strong methodology, and were published in a peerreviewed journal between 2019 and 2024. Conversely, exclusion criteria were applied to eliminate irrelevant articles, such as those that focused only on summative assessment, did not provide empirical data, or had weak methodologies.",
